    {
      "id": "S03",
      "title": "Bounded connection-error retry in callLLM",
      "intent": "Add a bounded retry-with-backoff for connection-class APICallError failures inside the callLLM wrapper. callLLM retries generateText when the thrown error ducks as name === 'AI_APICallError', isRetryable === true, and no numeric statusCode. Retry count and base delay come from env knobs OPENMAIC_LLM_CONNECTION_RETRIES (default 2) and OPENMAIC_LLM_CONNECTION_RETRY_BASE_MS (default 1000), with exponential backoff. Abort signals stay respected. Usage accounting, thinking resolution, LLM_THINKING_DISABLED, and streamLLM stay unchanged. On exhaustion callLLM throws an error preserving name AI_APICallError with the original as cause and a message that tells the agent to retry the call.",
      "user_stories": [
        1
      ],
      "blocked_by": [],
      "targets": [
        {
          "path": "lib/ai/llm.ts",
          "symbols": [
            {
              "name": "callLLM",
              "kind": "function",
              "expectation": "A transient connection-class AI_APICallError followed by success resolves with the successful text. A persistent connection-class AI_APICallError surfaces a message containing 'Retry the call' after the bounded budget, and only after the configured attempt count. A non-connection error is not retried, including an APICallError that carries a numeric statusCode. The retry-exhausted error preserves the original message text and the original error as cause. Environment knobs of 0 retries disable the new retry path.",
              "before": {
                "exists": true,
                "kind": "function",
                "signature": "(\n  params: T,\n  source: string,\n  retryOptions?: LLMRetryOptions,\n  thinking?: ThinkingConfig,\n  // eslint-disable-next-line @typescript-eslint/no-explicit-any\n): Promise<GenerateTextResult<any, any>>"
              },
              "postcondition": {
                "exists": true,
                "kind": "function",
                "signature": "(params: T, source: string, retryOptions?: LLMRetryOptions, thinking?: ThinkingConfig): Promise<GenerateTextResult<any, any>>"
              },
              "postcondition_quality": "INSPECTED"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "riskTier": 3,
      "uuid": "fc483550-d41b-426e-95cc-4b96b4bd602b",
      "impl": {
        "status": "pending",
        "hash": "a839711b15b8e9862282ec0ed1034f134efb54b5d9969e66ea285babef923d4a"
      },
      "verification": {
        "status": "pending",
        "hash": "a839711b15b8e9862282ec0ed1034f134efb54b5d9969e66ea285babef923d4a"
      },
      "expectation": "callLLM retries connection-class AI_APICallError failures with env-tuned exponential backoff, resolves transient failures, and on exhaustion throws an error preserving name AI_APICallError and the original cause with a message containing 'Retry the call'. Errors carrying a numeric statusCode are not retried by the wrapper. Environment knobs of 0 retries disable the new retry path.",
      "gates": [
        {
